From 63a9fa76b7a5ac920f0f6bdf57dc8bb67edb2741 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PromethenDev <PromethenDev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 02:33:37 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 43/97] vulkan: CPU readback of GPU resolves under resolution
 scaling (upscaling blocker)

ReadbackGpuWrittenRange refused when draw resolution scaling was on, so the
retro-HBK fix (game hook at XGUntileSurface -> MakeGpuWritesVisibleToCpu) left
retro HBK black at 2x. Scaled resolves are now tracked with their exact ranges
and guest pixel size (separate from the host buffer element size), read from
the scaled resolve buffer with the existing resolve-downscale compute shader
(one sample per scale block, original 32x32-tiled layout) and written to guest
memory; exact unscaled GPU writes (memexport) keep the shared-memory path;
unknown-destination memexports keep the old invalidation. Scale 1 unchanged.

Gates (Linux, Attitude Era tag match, fixed 420/480 s entrance timeline):
2x PASS, retro HBK in colour, 9 scaled readbacks; 3x (3840x2160) PASS, same;
1x PASS, scaled path unused. v1 (whole unknown memexport marked unscaled) and
v2 (bpe used as pixel size) broke 2x output and were rejected.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
